Nextcloud's logo in NextcloudMailExtension

NextcloudMailExtension uses Nextcloud's logo mark. The logo is not covered by this
repository's MIT licence (LICENSE), and Nextcloud does not publish it under an
open licence.

"Nextcloud and the Nextcloud logo is a registered trademark of Nextcloud GmbH
in Germany and/or other countries." (Nextcloud's trademark guidelines)

NextcloudMailExtension is not made, endorsed or supported by Nextcloud GmbH, and is
not an official Nextcloud client.


Files that use the logo

- Design/Nextcloud_02-blue-logo_mark-only.svg
  The blue "mark only" logo from Nextcloud's logo resources, unchanged.
- Extension/Assets.xcassets/ToolbarIcon.imageset/nextcloud-mark.svg
  The same mark for the Mail toolbar button, without the editor's metadata and
  with padding around it.
- Design/nextcloud-mail-extension-clip.svg
  The project's own artwork made from the mark: the mark in white, with a
  paperclip hooked on it, for the app's icon.
- Design/nextcloud-mail-extension-clip-site.svg
  The same artwork with the mark in Nextcloud's blue, #0082C9, for the website.
- App/AppIcon.icon
  The app's icon, made with Icon Composer from
  Design/nextcloud-mail-extension-clip.svg, on a gradient of Nextcloud's brand
  colours, #0082C9 and #1CAFFF, as the icon of Nextcloud's macOS desktop client
  has them.
- site/media/images/nextcloud-mail-extension-clip-site.svg
  The website's icon, a copy of Design/nextcloud-mail-extension-clip-site.svg.
- site/media/images/nextcloud-mail-extension-clip-site.png
  The same artwork as a 1200 x 630 PNG on white, for the website's link
  previews.
- site/media/screenshots/mail-send-overview-annotated.png and
  site/media/screenshots/mail-send-popup.png
  Screenshots for the project's website, showing the extension's toolbar button,
  with the mark above, in Mail's message window.
- site/media/screenshots/server-dir.png
  A screenshot of Nextcloud's own page for a shared folder, with Nextcloud's
  logo and wording as the server shows them.


Sources

- Logo resources: https://nextcloud.com/press/#logo-resources
- Brand page, with the logo usage requirements: https://nextcloud.com/brand/
- Trademark guidelines, last updated 26 June 2024:
  https://nextcloud.com/trademarks/


Terms

Nextcloud's brand page says that its name, logo and trademarks are protected,
that it supports "fair use" of its marks where the use is descriptive and
implies no endorsement, and that it can revoke permission at any time. Fair use
is a legal doctrine, not a licence.

The trademark guidelines allow the logos "only on the Internet and only as a
link to nextcloud.com", and say that third-party apps "should not include a
Nextcloud mark in the name". This project uses the mark for its icons and has
Nextcloud in its name, which goes beyond that. The project asks Nextcloud GmbH
for permission through https://nextcloud.com/contact, and replaces the icons
and changes its name if Nextcloud GmbH objects.
